@startuml sequence-diagram
title Autonomous Incident Response Sequence in University Edge-Cloud Platform

autonumber
actor "Attacker / Compromised IoT" as Attacker
participant "Edge Network Tap" as EdgeTap
participant "Edge Detector (IsolationForest)" as EdgeDetector
participant "Identity Fusion Engine" as IdentityFusion
queue "Redis Stream Broker" as EventBus
participant "Cloud Policy Engine" as PolicyEngine
participant "SOAR Autonomous Executor" as SOAR
participant "University SDN Controller / Firewall" as Firewall

Attacker -> EdgeTap: Send malicious payload / port scan / anomaly stream
EdgeTap -> EdgeDetector: Stream raw telemetry packet features
EdgeDetector -> EdgeDetector: Classify flow anomaly (Score > 0.75)
EdgeDetector -> IdentityFusion: Enrich telemetry with IP/MAC
IdentityFusion -> IdentityFusion: Match Campus LDAP / Role context (e.g. Student BYOD)
IdentityFusion -> EventBus: Publish SecurityEvent (Stream: security:telemetry:stream)

EventBus -> PolicyEngine: Consume security event
PolicyEngine -> PolicyEngine: Evaluate threat matrix, confidence & impact
PolicyEngine -> EventBus: Publish MitigationPolicy (Stream: security:alerts:stream)

EventBus -> SOAR: Trigger Automated Playbook execution
SOAR -> Firewall: Execute active containment (Revoke token / Block IP / Quarantine VLAN)
Firewall --> SOAR: Return execution status (Success)
SOAR -> EventBus: Log MitigationResult for feedback loop
@enduml
